  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "This optional challenge is classified as Easy difficulty. If you\u2019re interested in completing it, read on. Otherwise, skip to the next step.  \n\nA <b>vertex</b> (plural: vertices) is a point in where the edges of shapes meet \u2014 like a corner. In Unity, <b>vertex snapping</b> is a feature that allows you to perfectly align the vertices of different GameObjects to one another by snapping them together. \n\nVertex snapping is a little tricky at first, which is why this is an optional challenge. However, if you master this skill, it can be very useful!"
